  "note": "Triennial election of the rural district council, polled 27 May 1908: \"in this division only was there any contest\". The members returned unopposed for Ballyshiel, Mullabrack and Tandragee Rural were not found and are not filed. No party labels are printed. Polled 27 May 1908 in Mullavilly Schoolhouse, declared on Thursday 28 May. Mr. Joyce, a fourth nominee, withdrew (Northern Whig, 9 May 1908, p. 10). \"The contest was one of the keenest in the division for a long time.\""
